# Storefront mobile performance (PageSpeed / Lighthouse)

Baseline lab (Sep 9 2026 **1:33 PM** GMT+10, mobile Slow 4G, Moto G Power, Lighthouse 13.4.1): Performance **51**, FCP **3.3s**, LCP **8.4s**, TBT **420ms**, SI **7.7s**, CLS **0**, total network **~14.5 MiB**. Field CrUX: no data. Full mapping: `docs/storefront-mobile-lighthouse-2026-09-09.md`. Goal: improve CWV without violating homepage Hero protection.

## Invariant

Mobile first paint and LCP must not wait on **unused** CDN fonts, **no-store** of every asset, or **entire-page** client bundles. Hero design (logo, HOT ITEM, motion, gradients) stays protected — optimize **how** assets load, not Hero look.

## Top lab insights to keep closing (from baseline)

| Insight | Order of magnitude |
|---------|-------------------|
| Render-blocking requests | ~3s |
| Inefficient cache lifetimes | ~10 MiB transferable waste |
| Enormous network payloads | ~14.5 MiB total |
| Unused CSS | ~361 KiB |
| Image delivery | ~263 KiB |
| JS execution / main-thread / long tasks | ~2–3.5s / 9 tasks |

## Do (cheap, high impact)

- **Fonts:** Load Google/machine fonts only on customize/stamp routes (`GoogleFontsLinks` + segment layouts). Root `app/layout.tsx` = `next/font` Inter only. Never re-add sitewide font CSS for printers.
- **JS:** Prefer `dynamic(() => import(...), { ssr: false })` for Swiper, heavy editors, admin-only widgets on public pages. Avoid new `'use client'` on whole routes when a small island suffices.
- **Images:** Sized/compressed sources; `loading="lazy"` below fold; avoid full-bleed remote Unsplash on first viewport when a same-origin asset exists. LCP image: prioritize (`fetchPriority`), don’t lazy if it is LCP.
- **Cache:** Do not add HTML `Cache-Control: no-store` for marketing pages. Public GETs (`site-config`, catalog) should allow short SWR / max-age where freshness allows — not `?cb=Date.now()` on every home mount unless required.
- **CSS/JS weight:** Don’t import full icon packs or Swiper effect CSS globally for one section. Tree-shake; route-split. Watch unused CSS (~361 KiB class of waste).
- **DOM:** Avoid huge client trees on `/` (long task / TBT). Cap lists; virtualize only if needed later. Prefer a single `<main>` landmark on storefront pages.
- **3rd parties:** No new render-blocking scripts in root layout without defer/async and a kill-switch.

## Do not

- “Fix LCP” by redesigning Hero / removing Framer / changing brand gradients (homepage-protection).
- Pull accounting-sandbox into storefront webpack.
- Fix only desktop; always assume **Moto G / Slow 4G** class devices.
- Ship a feature that adds **>100 KiB** gzipped to the `/` critical path without lazy-loading or a separate route.
- Treat a **1:33 PM baseline** PSI paste as a post-deploy result — remeasure after the mobile-perf deploy before claiming wins.

## Cousins to check before merge

Empty CMS cache (Hero placeholder wait), cold CDN, multiple hero slides, category tiles, newsletter footer, Header cart hydrate, `ContentStoreSupabaseSync` + catalog hydrate racing first paint, console errors on `/`, CSP hardening (separate from CWV).

## When touching `/` or root layout

1. Re-read this rule + `homepage-protection.mdc`.
2. Prefer layout/font/cache/dynamic-import changes over Hero JSX edits.
3. After meaningful perf work: PageSpeed Insights mobile on `https://www.selpic.com.au/` — note FCP/LCP/TBT/payload delta vs Sep 9 **1:33** baseline in the PR/commit body.
